 "comment": "OD Account is under Bank OD A/c, itself under Loans (Liability), so it is both a bank ledger and a party. Partner Pi Current is under Partner Current Accounts, a group under Capital Account. The book's bank list names only Bank A, which the test does not read. Both books give every ledger the same GUID, so a party's figure ids are the same in both. This book's party_identity table lists party_groups: Partner Current Accounts, Sundry Debtors again, Cash-in-Hand, and No Such Group (no group has that name). So g01 (partner against a debtor, no bank or cash line) is listed as a journal settlement; g02 (paid from the OD, naming Alpha Traders) and g03 (naming the OD) are listed; g04 names Petty Cash, now a party; g05 is not listed (the OD is a bank ledger); g06 names the partner's ledger, now a party. ko_groups_off is the same book without party_groups.",
